<title>SPAIN: Santander cuts prime by 50 b.p. to 8.50 pct.</title>
<headline>Santander cuts prime by 50 b.p. to 8.50 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish largest commercial bank Banco Santander said it was cutting its prime interest rate by 50 basis points to 8.50 percent effective on Monday.</p>
<p>In a statement, Santander also said it reduced its fixed mortgage rate to 8.75 percent from 9.50 percent. The consumer credit rate was reduced to 11.50 percent.</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
</text>
